### 20\. V10 Development Roadmap

I recommend splitting V10 into manageable engineering milestones. The existing production plan should remain intact, especially the Ring 0 prototype and Ring 1 playable area.

| Phase | Development               | Completion requirement                                             |
| ----- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| 1     | Audit existing world data | All current map and region systems documented                      |
| 2     | Coordinate calibration    | Existing map coordinates convert consistently into Unity positions |
| 3     | Region connectivity       | Region graph validated                                             |
| 4     | World map rendering       | Global, regional and local views functional                        |
| 5     | Fog of war                | Discovery and survey states saved                                  |
| 6     | Geography upgrade         | Elevation, rivers, mountains and coastlines supported              |
| 7     | Terrain rendering         | Biome materials and blending implemented                           |
| 8     | Streaming foundation      | Sector loading and unloading functional                            |
| 9     | Traversal network         | Roads, trails, bridges and route validation                        |
| 10    | Underground maps          | Five canonical layers connected                                    |
| 11    | Labyrinth navigation      | 120-floor map navigation integrated                                |
| 12    | Persistence               | Player discoveries and world changes saved                         |
| 13    | Developer studio          | Editing and validation tools available                             |
| 14    | Optimization              | Performance and memory budgets validated                           |
| 15    | Integration               | Existing quests, creatures, NPCs and traversal work correctly      |

### Recommended implementation order

Do not start by generating all 40 regions in high detail.

Instead:

* Audit the existing coordinate and region definitions.

* Implement the coordinate conversion without breaking existing references.

* Build a working map using the current canonical data.

* Complete the Ring 0 and Ring 1 geography.

* Test terrain streaming with the actual playable environment.

* Expand the same pipeline to additional regions.

* Add underground and labyrinth navigation.

* Complete optimization and persistence.

This will avoid creating a beautiful world map that does not correspond to the actual playable world.

