# AETHWYRD V10
# WORLD MAP, GEOGRAPHY, TERRAIN & WORLD STREAMING OVERHAUL

## PROJECT

Aethwyrd — Unity 6, URP, 3D, third-person, strictly single-player fantasy RPG.

## PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Upgrade Aethwyrd's existing world architecture into a detailed, scalable, geographically consistent, explorable world.

V10 must improve the actual world map, geographical representation, terrain systems, coordinate architecture, regional connectivity, underground navigation, streaming, persistence, and development tools.

This is an upgrade to Aethwyrd's existing world, not a replacement of its canonical geography.

## MANDATORY CANON PRESERVATION

Before implementation, inspect the repository and identify the current versions of all relevant world files, scripts, scenes, data definitions, and assets.

Preserve the established world specifications:

- 40 canonical surface regions.
- Five canonical underworld layers.
- The 120-floor Great Labyrinth.
- Existing regional names and identities.
- Existing progression rings.
- Existing terrain and feature definitions.
- Existing region coordinates and radii.
- Existing Ring 0 and Ring 1 production priorities.
- Existing Vesper and post-game world specifications.

Do not invent replacement regions, rename established locations, change geographical relationships without authorization, or create competing definitions for existing world systems.

All existing canonical data must remain compatible or receive a documented migration.

