Do not replace the world. Improve the world that already exists.

### My strongest recommendation

I would make coordinate calibration, the world map, and region connectivity the first three deliverables. Everything else depends on them.

A larger map is not automatically a better world. A better world is one where the geography, playable terrain, map representation, navigation, and save data all describe the same place.

The next sensible step is a file-by-file audit of the existing world implementation before deciding the final physical size. That will tell us whether Aethwyrd needs a larger world, more detailed regions, better streaming, or all three.
